# Machi

Machi is a clean-slate product. Kultrun in this repository is evidence, not a runtime dependency.

Canonical docs: `docs/machi/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/machi/ROADMAP.md`, `docs/machi/CONTRACTS.md`, `docs/machi/TELEMETRY.md`, `docs/machi/KULTRUN.md`.

Full standing instructions: `docs/machi/MACHI_LEAD_DEVELOPER.md`.

## Must

- Use exact hierarchy IDs (`0.3.1`, not only `0.3`).
- Inspect Kultrun before designing an equivalent capability; copy only proven, uncluttered units.
- Keep production code free of `import kultrun`.
- Kernel must not import adapters or future Blocks. Composition root (`machi.main`) wires adapters.
- Install (1.2.1) may import Kernel. It must not import adapters, Steward, Capacity, or later Blocks.
- Kernel does not own Install state-root policy (`MACHI_STATE_ROOT`, platform default, mkdir).
- Events are append-only facts, not operational state. Do not event-source Install/Plan/Admit.
- Inject journal/storage roots. Kernel does not choose the Install state root.
- Binding a path is not ownership. Do not implement 1.3.1, 1.1.1, or 1.4.1 during 1.2.1.
- Privacy classification is required on every EventRecord. Filesystem paths are not `public_ops`.
- Build `python tools/build_machi.py` before server tests. Never edit source on the server.
- One bounded Component increment at a time. Design for the next Blocks; do not build them.

## Must not

- Merge Machi into `kultrun` or Kultrun into `machi`.
- Implement 1.3.1+ or Blocks 2–9 during a 1.2.1 increment.
- Fabricate DeploymentWitness from live re-resolution.
- Encode a vLLM-only architecture or implement extra runtime adapters to prove a port.
